  Flow-channel fit point
  Zone 6 is the intended flow-channel fit point. The player has practiced movement, attack, and dodging, so one previous self adds a new challenge while relying on skills already learned. Keep the arena readable and begin with only one previous self.
  Pacing risks and mitigation
  Boredom risk: Zone 5 may feel unnecessary if it is too long or empty. Mitigation: keep the recovery space brief and make it a purposeful pause before the new threat.
  Anxiety/frustration risk: Zone 7 may overwhelm the player if too many enemies attack at once or the previous self is hard to distinguish. Mitigation: cap simultaneous threats, use clear visual differences, and leave space to read attacks.
  Difficulty sequence: 1.0 → 1.5 → 2.5 → 3.0 → 1.0 → 4.0 → 5.0 → 1.0.
